{
  "$schema": "./schema/abort_mode.schema.json",
  "design_notes": [
    "Table 9.8, in row order. \"Abort calls are quick group votes (5 s) unless the escape system fires automatically on vehicle breakup.\"",
    "Section 4.2 gives quick votes, \"abort or continue\" among them, 10 s; 9.8 gives abort calls 5 s. The 5 s of 9.8 is stored here.",
    "flight_phases (flight-phase IDs, not facts) is a reading of the When column by the data author: the design names no phase IDs. \"Before/at lift-off\" is F1 and F2, \"during first-stage flight\" and \"early engine-out\" F3 to F5, \"late in ascent\" F7, \"in orbit\" F8.",
    "requirements and outcomes restate the two columns as markers for Core. Only the first two rows need the escape system, so only crewed contracts (the ones with an escape-system vote) can use them."
  ],
  "vote": {
    "duration_s": 5,
    "automatic_on_vehicle_breakup": true
  },
